WEBVTT

00:02.980 --> 00:03.900
Yeah, totally.

00:03.900 --> 00:04.470
That's cool.

00:05.410 --> 00:06.480
Aren't you into that?

00:06.480 --> 00:07.600
<i>Okay, next!</i>

00:06.480 --> 00:12.490
<b>Nick</b>

00:07.600 --> 00:10.230
<i>In </i>Super Galactic Construction
Equipment<i> episode 20,</i>

00:10.230 --> 00:13.290
<i>what finishing attack does
Yunboger use while on the planet Dokachin?</i>

00:13.290 --> 00:14.120
That's obvious!

00:16.300 --> 00:18.820
On an infinite train line
that leads to dreams,

00:19.630 --> 00:24.290
with fangs that pulverize stone,
opening a path to the horizon of the universe,

00:25.680 --> 00:28.440
he travels 100 million light years.

00:29.600 --> 00:35.960
Take this! Cozmo Hydraulic Tornado Attack!

00:45.390 --> 00:49.200
<i>Correct! The key being
that it's not Cosmo, but Cozmo!</i>

00:49.200 --> 00:50.760
That's easy! So easy.

00:50.760 --> 00:53.650
For the man who binged
the entire show in three sleepless nights!

00:53.650 --> 00:56.780
<b>Nick</b>

00:53.650 --> 00:58.000
<i>Hmph. Looks like you're learning 
the ropes, Otaku Hero.</i>

00:58.380 --> 01:01.780
We met some older senpai
who really schooled us on stuff.

01:02.120 --> 01:05.360
Like how unbelievably vast
and deep the otaku world is

01:05.360 --> 01:07.420
and how far I still have to go.

01:07.420 --> 01:11.340
<b>Nick</b>

01:09.140 --> 01:11.340
<i>Your determination is admirable.</i>

01:11.340 --> 01:14.260
<i>Akiba isn't only what
you see on the surface.</i>

01:11.340 --> 01:14.590
Akihabara Fruit Market

01:11.340 --> 01:14.590
<b>TV/Radio Parts Specialty Store</b>

01:11.340 --> 01:14.590
<b>Electrical Meter Specialty Shop</b>

01:11.340 --> 01:14.590
<b>Central Diner</b>

01:11.340 --> 01:14.590
<b>Room Coolers</b>

01:14.260 --> 01:16.600
<i>A whole lot has changed over the years.</i>

01:14.590 --> 01:17.590
Kanda Matsuri

01:14.590 --> 01:17.590
<b>New Items
In Stock</b>

01:16.600 --> 01:19.910
<i>But that doesn't mean
the past is lost, either.</i>

01:17.590 --> 01:20.600
<b>Paradise</b>

01:17.590 --> 01:20.600
<b>Parts Specialists</b>

01:17.590 --> 01:20.600
Discount <b>PC Shop</b>

01:19.910 --> 01:23.120
<i>The otaku spirit piles up like falling snow,</i>

01:20.600 --> 01:23.600
Sky of
the Future

01:20.600 --> 01:23.600
Containing all the lost
original recordings!
Experience the journey
of Yunboger in music!
Pre-orders Begin
May, 5th

01:23.120 --> 01:26.960
<i>and its layers embrace the changing times.</i>

01:26.960 --> 01:30.540
Hey, that's the line
from Yunboger in episode 119, right?

01:30.540 --> 01:31.360
<i>Gah!</i>

01:31.360 --> 01:35.110
<b>Nick</b>

01:32.930 --> 01:34.060
<i>Oh, by the way,</i>

01:34.060 --> 01:35.120
You dodged the question!

01:35.120 --> 01:38.780
<i>No! I mean, I got some info
you might be interested in.</i>

01:38.780 --> 01:40.120
Info?

01:40.120 --> 01:44.680
<i>Well, just think of it
as an urban legend. Listen up...</i>

01:40.120 --> 01:45.000
<b>Nick</b>

03:16.960 --> 03:18.300
Shibuya?!

03:18.300 --> 03:19.340
Yeah.

03:19.340 --> 03:25.090
He said if we go to Shibuya, we should be
able to amplify your powers many times over.

03:25.090 --> 03:26.350
Amplify?

03:26.550 --> 03:29.440
But it's just an urban legend? Very fishy.

03:29.440 --> 03:31.830
Gobo-bo bobobo bobo.

03:29.960 --> 03:31.830
"Sounds too good to be true."

03:31.830 --> 03:34.240
How would they increase their powers anyway?

03:34.240 --> 03:37.880
There's a comrade hiding there
who can apparently make a special "drug."

03:37.880 --> 03:38.770
Gobo?

03:38.770 --> 03:39.360
Huh?

03:39.360 --> 03:41.870
Gobo! Gobobo bo bobo bo!

03:41.870 --> 03:45.000
He doesn't mean <i>that</i> kind of drug!

03:43.560 --> 03:45.770
And we're supposed to believe that?

03:45.770 --> 03:49.300
Besides, SSC is crawling around
everywhere outside of Akiba.

03:49.300 --> 03:51.120
How would we avoid getting caught?

03:51.120 --> 03:54.130
Good question. Let's use the subway.

03:54.120 --> 03:56.880
Hachiko Entrance

03:54.120 --> 03:56.880
Bus Terminal

03:54.120 --> 03:56.880
Shibuya Station

03:54.120 --> 03:56.880
East Entrance

03:54.460 --> 03:55.830
The subway?

04:08.360 --> 04:10.550
After Akihabara was locked down,

04:10.550 --> 04:13.770
the Ginza Line subway was sealed off
at Mitsukoshimae station.

04:13.770 --> 04:16.300
Trains there are routed back to Shibuya.

04:17.080 --> 04:20.580
The Mansei Bridge is directly
above the Ginza Line tracks.

04:21.030 --> 04:26.800
If we walk down the tunnel to Mitsukoshimae,
then it's just a straight shot to Shibuya.

04:29.000 --> 04:30.500
This is totally the hard way!

04:30.500 --> 04:33.830
It would be a breeze to dig
with magic instead.

04:34.370 --> 04:36.560
Anarchy-chan, when you
and the girls use magic,

04:36.560 --> 04:38.330
it draws too much attention.

04:38.330 --> 04:42.300
Yeah, right! I bet you just
wanted to role play <i>The Great Escape</i>.

04:42.300 --> 04:43.060
Gobo gobo.

04:43.060 --> 04:44.260
N-No, I didn't!

04:44.610 --> 04:47.920
Ugh, all this digging makes my hips jiggle.

05:12.340 --> 05:14.720
Does this look right to you?

05:14.720 --> 05:19.180
Shibuya used to be packed
with all different types of people.

05:19.180 --> 05:21.470
Now everyone looks the same.

05:21.470 --> 05:23.970
Gobo... bo.

05:21.940 --> 05:23.960
"There are so many people, I wanna puke."

05:24.170 --> 05:26.170
D-Don't do it, Pink-chan!

05:26.170 --> 05:27.880
Don't hurl inside your mask!

05:30.980 --> 05:32.350
Hold it!

05:32.350 --> 05:34.220
I-I told you I'm not an otaku!

05:34.220 --> 05:36.860
Protection target spotted
in Shibuya jurisdiction! In pursuit!

05:38.320 --> 05:39.360
Secured!

05:39.810 --> 05:42.480
Hatobaya

05:39.810 --> 05:42.480
Sky of
the Future

05:41.110 --> 05:42.610
Th-That isn't mine!

05:45.000 --> 05:46.240
Bad idea.

05:46.240 --> 05:48.470
You know what happens if you get caught.

05:50.360 --> 05:53.600
I'll save him, too. Someday I'll save him.

05:53.600 --> 05:56.240
Wow, otaku still aren't extinct.

05:56.240 --> 05:57.660
What a nuisance.

05:57.660 --> 06:01.480
You can always tell one's close
from the smell and dirt.

06:01.480 --> 06:02.550
Go-bobo...

06:02.550 --> 06:03.130
What?

06:03.130 --> 06:04.920
Gobo gobo gobo. Gobo.

06:04.920 --> 06:06.250
"Otaku Hero-sama."

06:07.760 --> 06:09.510
<b>Shibuya Center-Gai</b>

06:11.020 --> 06:13.760
Surveillance cameras.

06:13.760 --> 06:16.020
Easy Measure Mode

06:13.810 --> 06:16.020
Otaku Quotient

06:14.430 --> 06:15.100
<b>Reading</b>

06:16.020 --> 06:18.150
Wait a minute! I'm really not an otaku!

06:18.150 --> 06:19.270
What is that?

06:19.490 --> 06:21.040
They're measuring otaku quotients.

06:21.040 --> 06:23.270
If they point that at us, we're done!

06:23.270 --> 06:24.220
We'd better go.

06:24.220 --> 06:24.990
Yeah.

06:33.460 --> 06:37.490
There's a "Chogo Master" around
here who's supposed to make the drug.

06:37.490 --> 06:38.660
Chogo Master?

06:38.660 --> 06:40.940
Every line of this is suspicious, huh?

06:40.940 --> 06:42.170
Kyu-chan, stay down.

06:42.170 --> 06:45.090
Which building?
They all look like massage parlors.

06:45.090 --> 06:45.940
Hey.

06:48.420 --> 06:51.050
You're otaku, aren't you?

06:51.050 --> 06:52.540
Hello, nice guy!

06:52.540 --> 06:54.640
Uh, we are ippanjin, not geeks.

06:54.640 --> 06:57.400
Just a group of common sense
folks who wouldn't hurt a fly.

06:57.400 --> 06:58.850
Gobo bobo bo!

06:58.850 --> 07:01.140
You're gonna give us away like that!

07:01.140 --> 07:03.930
That's the most otaku talk ever!

07:07.690 --> 07:09.120
You don't mean you...

07:09.120 --> 07:10.200
You're a closeted otaku?

07:10.200 --> 07:11.320
Yes!

07:11.320 --> 07:14.740
Nice to meet you! Myself is Markus, ne.

07:14.740 --> 07:16.080
Markus?

07:16.080 --> 07:19.440
And how! You my brother! Whoo!

07:19.440 --> 07:22.500
And those sisters are otaku, too, da ne?

07:21.940 --> 07:22.500
Huh?

07:22.500 --> 07:23.880
It-It's not...

07:23.880 --> 07:24.840
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

07:25.020 --> 07:27.710
Fishy behavior too weird to cover up.

07:27.710 --> 07:30.150
Odd kinks that let off strong stinks.

07:30.720 --> 07:31.880
Did I get something on me?

07:31.880 --> 07:34.680
And a masked maiden
who can't hold back the crazy!

07:33.790 --> 07:34.680
Gobo?

07:34.680 --> 07:36.530
Di-Di-Ding! On the nose!

07:36.530 --> 07:38.940
No mistake here,
you're the same as myself!

07:38.940 --> 07:41.960
Oh, gee! He saw right through us.

07:41.960 --> 07:43.870
And he's a foreigner, too!

07:43.870 --> 07:47.150
Gobo gobo!

07:44.560 --> 07:47.150
"I guess that means
we're totally global now."

07:47.590 --> 07:49.180
Exactly!

07:49.590 --> 07:52.690
This is sus. Thoroughly sus.

07:52.690 --> 07:53.660
Hum, hum?

07:53.660 --> 07:56.590
You were just thinking myself
to be "sus," were not you?

07:56.590 --> 07:57.080
Huh?

07:57.080 --> 07:59.230
Ah! N-No, I wasn't at all!

07:59.230 --> 08:00.330
It's fine desu.

08:00.720 --> 08:03.720
Ever since they started hunting otaku,

08:03.720 --> 08:07.850
myself had to hide my otaku
in the crowds of Shibuya.

08:07.850 --> 08:10.810
It had been so long since
myself had encountered my peeps,

08:10.810 --> 08:12.850
myself just had to say something.

08:13.270 --> 08:14.960
Is that what happened?

08:14.960 --> 08:15.920
You see?

08:15.920 --> 08:16.960
Y-Yes.

08:16.960 --> 08:18.960
Okay, good guy.

08:18.960 --> 08:22.560
Any otaku come wandering around
these parts wanna see Chogo Master.

08:22.560 --> 08:23.380
Don't you?

08:25.280 --> 08:27.360
Come on. Follow me.

08:27.360 --> 08:29.940
<b>Units Available
Taniguchi Bldg. #2</b>

08:30.260 --> 08:32.130
Koko is the building.

08:31.070 --> 08:35.490
<b>Taniguchi Bldg. #2</b>

08:32.640 --> 08:35.490
Myself has to split with you-tachi here.

08:35.490 --> 08:36.970
You're my bros!

08:36.970 --> 08:39.380
You get in a pinch, I'll come a-running, ne!

08:39.380 --> 08:40.400
Good luck.

08:40.400 --> 08:42.280
S-Sure!

08:47.130 --> 08:49.130
<b>Cabaret</b>

08:58.680 --> 08:59.830
This is it.

09:09.870 --> 09:10.920
What is this stuff?

09:11.280 --> 09:13.400
Ancient otaku artifacts?

09:14.030 --> 09:15.020
What's this?

09:15.020 --> 09:16.400
Hands off.

09:18.410 --> 09:20.850
That's a valuable Soviet vacuum tube.

09:20.850 --> 09:22.030
Soviet?

09:22.030 --> 09:23.480
Vacuum tube?

09:24.120 --> 09:26.160
Youngsters don't know crap.

09:26.370 --> 09:29.630
Even otaku have things they don't know.

09:30.290 --> 09:31.800
Otaku?

09:35.380 --> 09:37.310
So you're otaku, then?

09:38.560 --> 09:40.000
What's with this geezer?

09:40.000 --> 09:41.560
You're saying you're not?

09:41.560 --> 09:42.930
I'm not.

09:42.930 --> 09:46.230
I'm a "maniac."

09:46.230 --> 09:49.280
Maniac? Are you Chogo Master?

09:49.280 --> 09:50.730
The one and only.

09:50.730 --> 09:52.240
I'm Otaku Hero.

09:52.240 --> 09:53.730
And these are magical girls.

09:53.730 --> 09:55.730
I thought I said hands off!

09:55.730 --> 09:56.690
What's this?

09:56.690 --> 09:57.990
A crystal radio.

09:57.990 --> 09:59.230
Then what's this?

09:59.230 --> 10:01.990
Telegraph. Sends Morse code.

10:01.990 --> 10:03.050
Gobo-bo?

10:03.050 --> 10:04.160
Control line.

10:04.160 --> 10:06.760
Wired plane model from before RC.

10:07.890 --> 10:09.490
Awesome!

10:09.990 --> 10:13.160
The spirit piles up like falling snow,

10:13.160 --> 10:18.060
and its layers embrace the changing times...

10:19.280 --> 10:22.960
Chogo Master, seeing as you're
a first-rate otaku—

10:21.540 --> 10:22.960
Not an otaku!

10:24.260 --> 10:27.310
Seeing as you're a first-rate
maniac, I have a request.

10:27.310 --> 10:30.480
I want you to make a drug
to make these girls stronger!

10:30.480 --> 10:31.410
Oh, dear.

10:31.410 --> 10:35.270
I don't know what stories you were fed,
but I can't do nothing like that.

10:35.270 --> 10:35.980
Huh?

10:35.980 --> 10:38.670
All this trouble for nothing.

10:38.670 --> 10:39.360
Gobo?

10:39.360 --> 10:41.740
Gobo gobo...

10:39.360 --> 10:41.740
"I think I smell drugs."

10:42.900 --> 10:43.870
You've got tons!

10:46.110 --> 10:47.650
Come on! I'm begging!

10:47.650 --> 10:51.260
You must realize how
messed up the world is now.

10:51.260 --> 10:54.640
We're going to take Shobon down!
That's why the drugs—

10:53.370 --> 10:54.640
I refuse.

10:54.640 --> 10:58.140
I don't care about the world.
I just want to live here quietly.

10:58.140 --> 10:59.880
Are you really okay with that?

11:00.290 --> 11:02.840
This is all stuff you love, right?

11:02.840 --> 11:04.140
We're the same way.

11:04.140 --> 11:07.640
We want to live around the things we love
and show everyone we love them!

11:07.640 --> 11:08.560
You have to understand!

11:15.290 --> 11:17.410
A magazine clipping?

11:17.410 --> 11:18.150
What's this?

11:18.150 --> 11:26.280
<b>Japanese Treasure Found!</b>

11:18.150 --> 11:26.280
<b>The Ultimate Model
Becomes a Miraculous Item</b>

11:18.150 --> 11:26.280
<b>A unique set of magical girl figurines
produced by top figurine maker
Heino Production has been discovered.</b>

11:18.360 --> 11:23.300
Only one set was made, but it fell into
the hands of SSC during the otaku hunts.

11:23.300 --> 11:24.460
A legendary artifact.

11:24.460 --> 11:26.290
They're just magical girl dolls.

11:26.600 --> 11:28.800
Guess you're into them, too, huh, Gramps?

11:28.800 --> 11:29.770
Shut up!

11:29.770 --> 11:31.790
They look super old, though.

11:31.790 --> 11:35.640
Not as bad as the evil goddess,
but they look kind of shit.

11:35.640 --> 11:36.640
You aren't kidding.

11:36.640 --> 11:39.670
But you know, they are a little like us.

11:40.090 --> 11:42.430
So what do you want us to do?

11:49.920 --> 11:51.200
<i>Nakano?!</i>

11:51.200 --> 11:53.850
<i>That's right. We're heading there now.</i>

11:53.850 --> 11:54.860
<i>Give me the deets.</i>

11:56.620 --> 11:59.870
<i>After you destroyed it
in the Nakano Incident,</i>

11:59.870 --> 12:04.440
<i>SSC rebuilt it to be a warehouse
for confiscated items again.</i>

12:04.880 --> 12:08.040
<i>But the security's a hell of a lot worse now.</i>

12:08.040 --> 12:09.650
<i>But why, anyway?</i>

12:09.650 --> 12:12.180
Chogo Master wants to do an exchange.

12:12.180 --> 12:15.360
He said, "If you want the drugs,
bring me the legendary figurines."

12:15.360 --> 12:19.120
I know it's late to ask, but how do
we know they're in Nakano anyway?

12:19.120 --> 12:20.900
They could be in Akiba instead.

12:20.900 --> 12:24.240
I remember every last item
that we recovered in the Nakano Incident.

12:24.240 --> 12:25.640
This wasn't one of them.

12:25.850 --> 12:26.810
Are you serious?

12:26.810 --> 12:28.880
Otaku Hero-sama is insane!

12:29.480 --> 12:32.890
<i>Next is Nakano. Nakano.</i>

12:30.360 --> 12:33.690
<i>That thing is probably
on the top floor of Sunplaza.</i>

12:33.690 --> 12:35.020
Will you come help, Nick?

12:35.020 --> 12:38.020
<i>Hell no! I'm not setting foot outside Akiba.</i>

12:38.020 --> 12:39.650
But I'm counting on you!

12:40.470 --> 12:43.430
<i>Nakano. Nakano.</i>

12:41.240 --> 12:43.430
<i>Sorry, man. That ain't for me.</i>

12:43.430 --> 12:44.410
Nick!

12:44.760 --> 12:46.410
<i>Otaku Hero.</i>

12:47.180 --> 12:48.600
<i>Don't get yourself killed.</i>

12:50.790 --> 12:53.440
I guess we're back to raise hell again.

12:53.440 --> 12:54.380
Yeah.

12:54.380 --> 12:57.000
This is where we lit
the flames of revolution.

12:57.000 --> 12:59.280
I never expected to return.

12:59.280 --> 13:01.460
Gobo bobo bobo bo.

12:59.580 --> 13:01.460
"I'd give my life for drugs."

13:01.460 --> 13:03.670
One of us is here for the wrong reason.

13:03.830 --> 13:05.790
This time, it's fine.

13:05.790 --> 13:09.320
If we don't show our true stuff,
we'll never conquer that!

13:12.240 --> 13:13.560
There's no one here at all.

13:13.740 --> 13:16.810
Strange. Security is
supposed to be really tight.

13:20.710 --> 13:22.180
Sizzle.

13:24.920 --> 13:25.950
I was right.

13:26.170 --> 13:28.820
It's a weaponized building
with completely automated defenses.

13:28.820 --> 13:30.700
Did you need to roast me for that?

13:30.900 --> 13:32.790
We can't attack head-on,

13:32.790 --> 13:35.570
and flashy magic spells
would attract attention.

13:35.570 --> 13:37.720
We gotta go in low and quiet.

13:37.720 --> 13:40.260
Attack!

13:37.720 --> 13:40.260
Gobo!

13:48.970 --> 13:50.810
<i>A new morning arrives.</i>

13:51.370 --> 13:55.930
<i>But the sparkle it brings
to us is not a ray of hope.</i>

13:56.460 --> 13:58.880
<i>The pitch-black darkness obscuring our path</i>

13:58.880 --> 14:01.900
<i>has merely been replaced
with a frozen pure white.</i>

14:01.900 --> 14:04.640
I know you're trying
to be all dramatic and stuff,

14:04.640 --> 14:07.480
but was Nakano Sunplaza always this tall?

14:07.480 --> 14:10.410
How would I know?
Either way, we gotta climb.

14:19.770 --> 14:21.620
Thank you, Blue-chan!

14:21.620 --> 14:24.920
I'm so glad I got your left leg!

14:24.920 --> 14:27.270
It'd be so much harder
if I caught the middle one.

14:27.270 --> 14:29.260
It hurts to just hear that!

14:29.840 --> 14:31.270
<i>Second day of the attack.</i>

14:30.300 --> 14:33.260
<b>- Second Day -</b>

14:31.710 --> 14:33.270
<i>The summit is yet far away.</i>

14:35.730 --> 14:37.140
Otaku Hero!

14:37.140 --> 14:37.760
What's wrong?

14:38.360 --> 14:41.020
Kyo-chan... isn't breathing.

14:42.090 --> 14:44.520
<i>The gods of the mountain know no mercy.</i>

14:44.700 --> 14:48.870
<i>They test us with relentless trials
and beckon us to the world beyond.</i>

14:49.390 --> 14:51.030
<i>Starting with the weakest of us.</i>

14:52.030 --> 14:56.700
I bet Kyo-chan was dreaming
of eating hot stew by a warm fireplace.

14:59.280 --> 15:02.520
<i>Saying farewell to our departed
is yet another trial.</i>

15:02.520 --> 15:04.120
I'll get rid of this junk.

15:08.190 --> 15:10.680
<i>How many days had passed?</i>

15:10.680 --> 15:15.040
<i>We were already struggling to stay
conscious when it finally happened.</i>

15:16.680 --> 15:19.040
<i>We completely ran out of food.</i>

15:19.380 --> 15:21.720
<i>The gods of the mountain know no mercy.</i>

15:22.200 --> 15:26.410
<i>They test us with cold and hunger
and beckon us to the underworld.</i>

15:26.410 --> 15:28.700
<i>Starting with the least devoted.</i>

15:28.700 --> 15:31.700
It's over. I'm starving.

15:31.700 --> 15:34.200
Keep it together.

15:34.370 --> 15:38.590
I'm at my limit.
I just want a bite of something.

15:38.590 --> 15:40.080
Gobo-bo.

15:40.080 --> 15:42.560
We don't have anything to eat.

15:42.560 --> 15:43.860
Not a thing.

15:57.350 --> 15:59.980
<b>- Third Day -</b>

16:00.940 --> 16:01.720
Look out!

16:03.490 --> 16:05.470
Brreyouegh!

16:08.230 --> 16:10.990
Hot, hot, hot, hot, hot,
hot, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot!

16:10.990 --> 16:13.240
I'm sledding!

16:19.780 --> 16:22.920
<i>Does the peak we seek truly await us?</i>

16:22.920 --> 16:26.810
<i>Or is this path to heaven instead
leading us on a road to hell?</i>

16:26.810 --> 16:28.380
<i>The doubt is unshakable.</i>

16:28.380 --> 16:31.100
<i>Are we chasing a phantom that doesn't exist?</i>

16:32.130 --> 16:33.160
<i>That's when it happened.</i>

16:33.160 --> 16:35.000
Otaku Hero, look!

16:35.640 --> 16:38.290
The peak! It's the peak, Otaku Hero-sama!

16:38.290 --> 16:39.440
Gobo bobo bo!

16:39.440 --> 16:41.010
Let's go, Otaku Hero!

16:41.010 --> 16:41.640
Yeah!

16:47.550 --> 16:50.680
<i>It was almost within our reach.</i>

16:50.680 --> 16:52.370
<i>But they know no mercy.</i>

16:54.200 --> 16:56.520
<i>Is that... a god?</i>

17:03.550 --> 17:04.660
Markus?!

17:04.660 --> 17:06.820
In a pinch, I came a-running.

17:06.820 --> 17:07.920
Told you, ne.

17:07.920 --> 17:09.400
Markus!

17:11.300 --> 17:14.800
Up-a-see daisy!

17:14.800 --> 17:16.730
Thank you, Markus!

17:16.730 --> 17:18.170
I'm sorry I doubted you.

17:18.170 --> 17:19.810
Don't touch my mustache!

17:21.140 --> 17:22.580
Otaku Hero.

17:22.930 --> 17:24.690
This is the top floor, isn't it?

17:24.690 --> 17:25.950
It's okay to transform, right?

17:25.950 --> 17:26.680
Gobo.

17:26.680 --> 17:29.480
Yeah! Put on a show, girls!

17:29.480 --> 17:33.440
Aw yeah! Japanese magical girls is cool!

17:33.440 --> 17:34.700
Transform!

17:33.440 --> 17:34.700
Gobo!

18:17.360 --> 18:18.360
<b>Transform</b>

18:26.250 --> 18:26.620
<b>Self-Righteousness</b>

18:27.040 --> 18:27.410
<b>Hope</b>

18:28.290 --> 18:28.670
<b>Love</b>

18:29.370 --> 18:29.870
<b>Transience</b>

18:34.300 --> 18:35.380
<b>Transformation Complete</b>

18:37.840 --> 18:41.590
<b><b>Type 99 Antipersonnel Security Perimeter
Type 02 Antipersonnel Laser Mines</b></b>

18:38.680 --> 18:41.320
<i>Intruders detected! Intruders detected!</i>

18:41.320 --> 18:43.840
<i>Activate Armageddon Mode and intercept.</i>

18:41.590 --> 18:43.850
<b><b>Type 98 Building Defensive Armament
Saturation Attack Specification (Armageddon Mode)</b></b>

18:43.840 --> 18:45.890
<i>Activate Armageddon Mode and intercept.</i>

18:51.060 --> 18:52.190
Gobo-bo!

18:55.810 --> 18:57.090
Amazing!

18:57.090 --> 18:58.820
Get 'em, Anarchy-chan!

19:09.260 --> 19:10.250
Gobo!

19:10.730 --> 19:11.580
Gobo!

19:15.250 --> 19:16.500
There's still more!

19:30.720 --> 19:31.390
Ouch.

19:31.390 --> 19:33.350
That's our Anarchy-chan.

19:33.350 --> 19:35.130
Oh, that's it!

19:35.440 --> 19:37.190
Go, Anarchy-chan!

19:37.190 --> 19:39.650
Oh, yeah!

19:43.710 --> 19:44.590
Smash it open!

19:44.590 --> 19:46.460
Please stop!

19:45.310 --> 19:46.460
Help me!

19:47.210 --> 19:49.450
It hurts! It hurts!

19:47.500 --> 19:49.450
Stop it!

19:48.670 --> 19:49.450
Huh?

19:49.450 --> 19:50.610
The pain!

19:50.610 --> 19:52.520
It hurts! It hurts!

19:52.520 --> 19:53.960
I can't take it!

19:53.960 --> 19:55.110
What the hell?

19:55.110 --> 19:56.420
Gobo bobo-go.

19:55.110 --> 19:56.420
"That's nasty."

19:57.210 --> 19:59.470
Are these all captured otaku?

19:59.470 --> 20:00.770
Is that even possible?

20:00.770 --> 20:03.590
Are these myself's buddies?! My God!

20:05.070 --> 20:08.360
If they are, I can't hurt them.

20:08.360 --> 20:11.870
Damn it! How can we save them?

20:12.870 --> 20:16.420
It's fine! Just let us die in peace.

20:16.420 --> 20:18.360
Next time, I'll be reborn a normal—

20:18.360 --> 20:20.450
Hoo!

20:19.610 --> 20:20.440
Wha—?!

20:20.440 --> 20:21.360
Pink-chan?!

20:23.160 --> 20:25.600
Otaku are just, otaku are just,

20:25.600 --> 20:28.040
ota, ota, ota, o-o-ota...

20:28.040 --> 20:28.960
Gross!

20:28.960 --> 20:30.620
These are all fakes!

20:30.620 --> 20:31.370
Anarchy-chan!

20:31.370 --> 20:32.300
Yeah!

20:32.300 --> 20:37.610
Heaven's Judgment Day!

20:53.650 --> 20:54.650
Gobo.

21:00.770 --> 21:02.570
Is this the right one?

21:02.570 --> 21:04.570
Yes. Definitely.

21:04.770 --> 21:09.700
How exquisite. The lines, the details.

21:09.700 --> 21:11.720
It truly is the ultimate in molding—

21:11.720 --> 21:12.820
Gobo!

21:12.820 --> 21:25.350
Gobo gobo! Gobo gobo!

21:14.680 --> 21:17.450
I hate to spoil the moment,
but the loony here is saying,

21:17.450 --> 21:19.600
"hand over the stuff you owe."

21:19.600 --> 21:21.920
The drugs that will make us stronger.

21:24.640 --> 21:25.350
Here.

21:28.040 --> 21:29.120
Is this it?

21:29.120 --> 21:31.010
You did make it for us!

21:31.010 --> 21:32.880
So he actually believed in us.

21:32.880 --> 21:33.590
Gobo gobo.

21:33.590 --> 21:34.240
"Tsundere."

21:34.240 --> 21:35.480
Shut up!

21:35.880 --> 21:37.770
Thank you, Chogo Master.

21:37.770 --> 21:39.560
We definitely won't waste them.

21:39.560 --> 21:42.310
Once the world changes,
come over and visit us

21:42.720 --> 21:44.360
in our Akiba.

21:44.360 --> 21:45.760
Now get the hell out.

21:45.760 --> 21:47.370
You're wearing out your welcome.

21:48.740 --> 21:50.990
Thank you, Chogo Master!

21:50.990 --> 21:52.470
Pleasure doin' business.

21:52.470 --> 21:53.490
Gobo bo.

22:01.480 --> 22:06.510
Gobo bobo! Go bobobobo!

22:03.600 --> 22:06.500
"Let's take them! Let's use them now!"

22:06.500 --> 22:08.090
Nope. I'll hang onto them.

22:08.580 --> 22:09.970
Huh? Why?

22:09.970 --> 22:13.200
We might face even stronger
enemies down the road.

22:13.560 --> 22:16.230
Gotta save our trump card
for the right moment.

22:16.230 --> 22:18.960
Gobo, gobo...

22:18.960 --> 22:25.250
Gobo! Gobobobo! Go-bobo bobo bo-gobo!

22:27.930 --> 22:30.360
Nakano has fallen again?

22:30.360 --> 22:31.470
Yeah.

22:31.470 --> 22:32.620
Shobon-sama!

22:32.620 --> 22:33.750
No worries.

22:33.750 --> 22:34.520
But!

22:34.520 --> 22:35.730
Slayer.

22:36.240 --> 22:38.420
Everything is fine.

22:43.330 --> 22:44.290
Dad!

22:45.390 --> 22:46.550
Kathy!

22:47.300 --> 22:49.720
Dad! Dada!

22:50.170 --> 22:51.640
Kathy...

22:55.130 --> 22:57.060
That was some real nice work.

22:57.060 --> 22:59.520
I doubt they noticed a thing.

22:59.520 --> 23:01.770
You've fulfilled your role.

23:01.770 --> 23:05.400
Take these and leave the country today.

23:05.400 --> 23:07.660
Very well done.

23:26.130 --> 23:28.840
Yesterday's foes are also today's foes.

23:28.840 --> 23:30.460
A never-ending battle.

23:30.460 --> 23:33.550
One long night when it all began,

23:33.550 --> 23:35.810
the girls awakened.

23:35.810 --> 23:39.080
A miracle on an eve long ago.
